{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526031-quick-question-on-how-werewolfs-handle-currupted-sprits","id":1526031,"title":"Quick question on how werewolfs handle Currupted sprits.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-27T19:57:19-08:00","id":1526031,"title":"Quick question on how werewolfs handle Currupted sprits.","content":"Ya, i am running a very unique game. I wont go into too many details but the party has a group of Gauro who play a non violent role in the story. That said i intend for them to go after a Corrupted spirit. This spirit of the wild was tainted by the city and the Decay of the buildings it resides in. Which is an empty office building that only exist as more or less a tax write off. So it languages in an empty decaying building.<br /> <br /> My question is how would they handle this? Would they aim to destroy the sprite or is their any other way they could untainted it? as i am not a 100% familiar with the WTA system. But it plays a direct role in the story so i cannot avoid it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13272-rman88","name":"rman88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T20:36:05-08:00","id":1526033,"title":"","content":"I think the general preference for the Garou would be to redeem the spirit before destroying the spirit. (I am not sure what you mean by destroy. Battling the spirit so it has zero Essence means it merely goes into slumber and will eventually awake again once it recovers all Essence. Actually permanent destroying the spirit requires the Garou to harvest enough of its Gnosis, but that is a rule frequently overlooked.) But that is just a general preference. A lot depends on the specifics of the spirit, its corruption, and the attitude of the local tribes and septs (and pack totems). Children of Gaia and Stargazers who belong to a sept of a Caern of Healing will put a lot more effort into trying to redeem a spirit than the Get of Fenris pack whose pack totem is Boar at a sept whose Caern is of Rage.<br /> <br /> However, I do not think there are any mechanics to uncorrupt a corrupted spirit. You can't simply use the right Gift or Rite and make it uncorrupted. It would have to be a story thing that the ST requires. It shouldn't be so hard as to be impossible, but it also shouldn't be so easy that there isn't any reason why Garou are not doing this all the time.<br /> <br /> If I wanted to run a plot where the PCs could redeem such a spirit, I would break it down into several actions for them to do.<br /> <br /> First, figure out why the spirit is corrupted. Something had to happen. Once you know why it turned to the Wyrm, you can figure out some means where it could be uncorrupted. That might require the PCs to go on spirit quests, use Enigmas for dream/omen interpretations, use Gifts like Sight from Beyond, interview other spirits who are witnesses to what happened, etc.<br /> <br /> Second, there is likely some place of Wyrm taint where the spirit first became corrupted or where it is dwelling now. The PCs would need to go there, remove or eliminate the source of corruption, and then perform the Rite of Cleansing to eliminate any residual Wyrm taint. So if there is a water or fish spirit in a waterway being corrupted as a result of pollution from nearby factory, the PCs would first need to find a way to permanently stop the pollution and then remove any still existing pollution from the water. Then once that happens, they can perform the Rite of Cleansing to eliminate the remaining spiritual Wyrm taint without fear it'll just come back immediately.<br /> <br /> Third, if there is another component to the spirit's corruption, they'll need to address that as well. For example, when the Bat Incarna fell, it wasn't because of any industrial pollution. It was from despair/anger over its children's destruction. That likely involves some kind of chiminage to appease the spirit which the ST will need to determine. Obviously, appeasing a Gaffling or Jaggling is much easier than what would be needed to appease an Incarna. But it will still require the PCs to approach the corrupted spirit and talk to it. Simply in order to approach it safely might require various things. It could include use of the Rite of Contrition. Maybe it involves the Rite of Summoning with all the danger that summoning a corrupted spirit might do. This could be the meat of the plot here so give it a lot of thought.<br /> <br /> Fourth, after whatever combination of the second and third steps are done by the PCs, you can now set up the finale. The PCs have dealt with all the issues that might have caused the spirit's corruption. Now they need to find the spirit, capture it, and perform a final Rite of Cleansing. While the PCs could subdue the spirit by force, I think it would be better to approach this in a non-violent manner if possible. Treat it less like combat and more like an intervention for a drug addict or alcoholic. Beating up someone who drinks too much or uses drugs so you can drag them to a treatment center is not likely going to help them give up their habit. This is about spiritually HEALING the spirit, not defeating it in combat.<br /> <br /> So here is where you would want to use Gifts like Command Spirit or Call to Duty or perhaps some Fetish. Or if the players like that, perhaps use some sort of bribery like providing Gnosis or performing more Chiminage. Then, having addressed the reasons you determined for its corruption, you can cleanse the spirit and redeem its nature.<br /> <br /> This should create a very strong tie between the spirit and the PCs. So I would make this spirit an ongoing NPC in the spirit world that interacts with the pack a lot going forward. As part of their efforts, the PCs should be taking the commitment to continue to watch out for the spirit and its spirit habitat so that it doesn't regress into being corrupted again.<br /> <br /> If your PC wants to do this, this should not be an encounter. This is probably the entire game session or perhaps even multiple game sessions. You'll want to make it challenging enough so that 1) they feel a real sense of accomplishment, and 2) it's enough of an effort that it is understandable why PCs or NPCs don't do this all the time. The less powerful a spirit (a local Gaffling), the less difficult this will be. The more powerful the spirit, the most difficult and more time consuming this should be. The trick is for you the ST to fine tune the efforts needed that best reflects the details of your chronicles and game.<br /> <br /> The above isn't a rule. It's just me brainstorming up a guideline. Hope this helps you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T23:12:55-08:00","id":1526038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1526031-quick-question-on-how-werewolfs-handle-currupted-sprits?p=1526033#post1526033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the general preference for the Garou would be to redeem the spirit before destroying the spirit. (I am not sure what you mean by destroy. Battling the spirit so it has zero Essence means it merely goes into slumber and will eventually awake again once it recovers all Essence. Actually permanent destroying the spirit requires the Garou to harvest enough of its Gnosis, but that is a rule frequently overlooked.) But that is just a general preference. A lot depends on the specifics of the spirit, its corruption, and the attitude of the local tribes and septs (and pack totems). Children of Gaia and Stargazers who belong to a sept of a Caern of Healing will put a lot more effort into trying to redeem a spirit than the Get of Fenris pack whose pack totem is Boar at a sept whose Caern is of Rage.<br /> <br /> However, I do not think there are any mechanics to uncorrupt a corrupted spirit. You can't simply use the right Gift or Rite and make it uncorrupted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ahem. Arguably The Malleable Spirit. Some spirits might not be wholly corrupted and might respond well to various rites, particularly Gurahl healing rites. You just need to get them to stand still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T03:53:37-08:00","id":1526048,"title":"","content":"Ok, this is all good to know. Thou i feel your not getting all the context to it. So let me set the scene if i could. First of all my game is Actual a Vampire the Masquerade story. The players are all freshly made kindred who are dealing with a crisis in New York City. The Former prince is dead and the new one is barely holding on as vultures circle overhead. And In comes a new player within the kindred community.<br /> <br /> This kindred who has been part of the undead for about 2 years. Has managed to reach a level few have seen in those who have lived over 100 years. This is because he answered the Call of A Mummy to deal with a world ending threat. He joined with the Gauro, Gurahl and Ajaba to deal with a reality breaking threat. And thus earned the favor of the spirits even thou he is a wyrm tainted individual. Thou he argues when it comes to the Wyrm and Kindred. Its more complicated as the kindred are not driven to destroy. But are more driven to survive at any cost. Which dose not align with say the Black Spiral Dancers or any Wyrm sprite who overall goal is to end the world. Thou this sentiment depends on kindred in question. As say the sabbot would more then willingly be used as pawns for the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Mind you i am taking liberties as i am not a 100% sure if any of this could be cannon. Regardless, after he went threw hell saving the world. His former pack disbanded and now he is working with a group of Gauro that he saved.Turns out if you use some vampire powers a bit more creatively then just as a hammer. They could be used for far greater and better purposes. And who could argue that the art of vicissitude couldn't be used to help people. In this case, to draw the wyrms taint out of the flesh. Giving momentarily celerity to those who could only truly be redeemed by a dip in the lake of silver.<br /> <br /> So now he leads the pack of the Redeemed. Former black spiral dancers who are looking for redemption for falling to the Wyrm. One way they do this is by helping the lost sprites traped in the Metal Jungle of this city. And thus i was going to have the players explore this aspect. As most of this is happening behind the scenes. As in truth he knows the players only reason for being their. Least originally is to spy on him for the prince. Which they are not really good at. But he also needs people to do buzzy work for him. So he dose not really mind to much.<br /> <br /> Regardless his goals for his pack is to aid the spirits of New York, while he figures out a way to cure their souls. Outside of just straight up dying in silver. This is why he is sending his pack to help cleanse the spirit lost in a maze of empty rooms. Alone in the darkness, with only the faint hum of decaying light bulbs to keep it company. All the while the humans who own this building. Are just using it as a tax write off. Which is actual a thing in New York.<br /> <br /> O, encase your wondering. The Kindred in question acts as more of a central quest giver and a Mystery for the players to solve. He dose not accompany the party around, unless their is a real reason for it. For example when he had them visit the Primogen of the Nosferatu. Who is the number 1 crime boss in New York city. And one of the players is a Malkavian who thinks he is a super hero and the other is a cop. He was their to make sure no one decided to get everyone killed because they had a issue with the morality of this situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13272,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13272-rman88","user":"rman88","date":". 11-28-2023, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13272-rman88","name":"rman88","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}